  "findings": "Learned circuit routing won five, lost three and was inconclusive in four of twelve primary BCE contrasts; three wins exceeded the 0.01 practical reference throughout their adjusted intervals. G121 remained much better on checkerboard and spiral. MLP4 led the descriptive Banknote check. Exact conversion preserved 276 circuit predictors and 1,380 expert cores.",
  "models_tasks": "Plan B compares hard geometric routing, fixed soft mixtures, learned soft mixtures, parameter-count-matched residual controls and G121. Four synthetic families use eight confirmation populations and two paired optimizer seeds. Banknote Authentication is a secondary fixed grouped split with five optimizer seeds and additional MLP2, MLP4 and LR2 controls.",
  "limits": "48 engineering, 72 development, 636 confirmation and four clean retraining fits. Banknote is one fixed split, not five independent datasets. Shared diagnostic numerical primitives, small-sample t assumptions, mixture costs, local timing and absent physical hardware constrain claims. The original top-level READ_ME.txt is a stale preparation notice; final report and acceptance records govern completion.",
